---
import Center from "../components/Center.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <Center>
    <div class="my-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">👨‍🏫 Personal Note on Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        Hello! 👋 I'm <a
          href="https://www.joshuapullen.com"
          class="font-semibold underline hover:decoration-dashed">Josh Pullen</a
        >, and I built Slide Stencil. The full legal text of the privacy policy
        is below, but I wanted to summarize the main points because it's
        difficult to make the legal text easily scannable. Here's the
        (non-legally binding) gist:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc text-lg mt-4 pl-8 space-y-2">
        <li class="pl-2">
          Slide Stencil does not collect any information about you.
        </li>
        <li class="pl-2">
          However, it is a Google Add-on, and Google collects all kinds of
          information about you. I don't control what they do.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Too good to be true?</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        If I was you, I'd be asking what the catch is. <em class="italic"
          >Why make this for free? Isn't the incentive always to collect more
          data?</em
        > Here's my business model:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal text-lg mt-4 pl-8 space-y-2">
        <li>
          I make tons of apps for teachers. Most of them are completely free.
        </li>
        <li>
          A few of my apps, like <a
            href="https://www.shufflebuddy.com/"
            class="font-semibold underline hover:decoration-dashed"
            >Shuffle Buddy</a
          >, have some paid features.
        </li>
        <li>The free apps help attract users to the paid apps.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        That's the whole business model. I think it's a win-win.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-400 my-8" />

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4 italic">Last updated: April 27, 2026</p>

      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        This Privacy Policy is a transparent explanation of how Slide Stencil
        ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and protects your information
        when you use the Google Workspace Add-on. By using Slide Stencil, you
        agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this
        policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Information We Collect</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        We do not collect any first-party personally identifiable information
        from users of the Slide Stencil Add-on. The add-on operates entirely
        within your Google Workspace environment, and we do not collect your
        data or documents. Your data is accessible only to Google, in accordance
        with their privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        The Slide-Stencil Add-on is built using the Google Apps Script platform,
        which is a third-party service provided by Google. All data collected by
        the add-on is processed and stored by Google in accordance with their
        privacy policies. We recommend reviewing Google's privacy policy for
        more information on how they handle data.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        Since we do not collect or store any first-party information, we do not
        use or share any data from our users. The only information processed by
        the add-on is handled exclusively by Google.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Data Security</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        Slide Stencil does not manage any user data. Instead, data storage and
        security is handled exclusively by Google. We recommend reviewing
        Google's security practices to understand how your data is protected
        when using the Slide Stencil Add-on.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Data Retention</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        Slide Stencil does not collect or store any user data, so we do not have
        any data retention policies. All data processed by the add-on is handled
        by Google, and we recommend reviewing Google's data retention policies
        for more information.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you
        of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page. You are
        advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.
        Changes to this Privacy Policy are effective when they are posted on
        this page.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mt-4">
        If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us
        via the <a
          href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc65YkfxbguqPhmHPmgm3CJ_oOkGOlPqXEB5hXyzcPrOKBCiA/viewform?usp=publish-editor"
          class="font-semibold underline hover:decoration-dashed"
          >contact form</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Center>
</Layout>
